Integer framebuffer sRGB output, default on since pass 58 (LD_SRGB_OUT=0 turns it off): NV4097_SET_SHADER_PACKER (0x1FEC) non-zero encodes the RGB of every colour export (linear to sRGB) when the program exports halves, on integer colour surfaces. Adapted from sp00nznet/ps3recomp PR #304 by tekulvw (RPCS3 RSXROPEpilogue semantics).

KZ3 sets 0x1FEC in ~15 % of the draws that sample a texture (pass 56 counter, patch 2054). The PR's engine splice does not apply to the live-draw path, so rsx_fp_apply_srgb_output renames the generated entry point to _rsx_main and appends a wrapper main that encodes t0..t3 (alpha and SV_Depth untouched); it runs after every other post-pass, works on both output shapes and leaves the source untouched on failure. rsx_fp_srgb_output_enabled (PR): packer != 0, not 32-bit exports (SHADER_CONTROL 0x40), surface format not 0x0B/0x0C/0x0D. The flag is part of the PSO key.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): partly absorbed, PR304 sRGB output in the decompiler, the D3D12 live-draw call site kept.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

